    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4238356/Benedictine-College/Advancement-Services-Coordinator": {
      "title": "Benedictine College - Advancement Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Benedictine College - Advancement Services Coordinator In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Advancement Services Coordinator Benedictine College Apply Advancement Services Coordinator Atchison, KS Apply Description Department: Advancement Job Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Reports To: Advancement Services Supervisor Grade/Level: Amount of Travel Required: None Work Schedule: Full-time, on-site Positions Supervised: None POSITION SUMMARY The Advancement Services Coordinator is a member of a dynamic team that collaborates to provide high-quality services and support to Advancement staff, alumni, donors, and other stakeholders. This position serves as a Data Steward for the Advancement database and supports Benedictine College's fundraising objectives through accurate data management, reporting, and constituent record stewardship. The successful candidate will thrive in a fast-paced, customer-focused environment and demonstrate strong analytical skills, attention to detail, persistence, initiative, and a commitment to data integrity. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing, with key stakeholders. Train colleagues on the efficient and consistent use of Raiser’s Edge. Utilize a consultative approach when working with colleagues to identify and provide information needed to support both short-term objectives and long-term success. Provide database and administrative support in the daily operation of the Advancement Office, including: Process gifts accurately and in a timely manner. Create, update, and inactivate constituent records. Perform database maintenance, updates, and record cleanup. Develop complex queries, exports, and reports. Generate mailing lists and data extracts. Prepare routine reports for department leadership and other stakeholders. Reconcile discrepancies across systems and databases. Import and export data to and from Raiser’s Edge. Run mail merges for monthly pledge reminders and other Advancement communications. Maintain updated constituent addresses through NCOA processing. Process event registrations and related data entry. Scan and maintain gift documentation. Attach and maintain supporting documentation within constituent records. Support Alumni and Advancement events as needed. Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements DEPARTMENTAL EXPECTATIONS: Maintain a professional, positive, and respectful attitude. Uphold strict confidentiality regarding donor, constituent, and College information. Demonstrate effective time management and organizational skills. Take ownership of assigned projects through completion. Apply data management principles to ensure information is accurate, complete, and consistent. Communicate effectively and collaborate with key stakeholders. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS Competency Statements Demonstrated proficiency with Raiser’s Edge (Database View and NXT), Virtuous, or another fundraising CRM system. Experienced user of Microsoft Excel, including advanced functions such as filters and sorting Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. High attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy. Ability to manage multiple priorities while meeting deadlines. Experience with Omatic, HubSpot, Microsoft Office, SharePoint, and MarketSmart is preferred. Education Bachelor’s degree in Business, Information Systems, Computer Science, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience Two or more years of experience working with Raiser’s Edge, Virtuous, or a comparable Fundraising CRM system. Knowledge of fundraising principles and practices PHYSICAL DEMANDS Physical Abilities Stand F Walk F Sit F Handling / Fingering F Reach Outward O Reach Above Shoulder O Climb O Crawl Squat or Kneel O Bend O Push / Pull 12 lbs or less F 13-25 lbs O 26-40 lbs O 41-100 lbs N Lift /Carry 10 lbs or less F 11-20 lbs O 21-50 lbs O 51-100 lbs N Over 100 lbs N N (Not Applicable) Activity is not applicable to this occupation. O (Occasionally) Occupation requires this activity up to 33% of the time (0 - 2.5+ hrs/day) F (Frequently) Occupation requires this activity from 33% - 66% of the time (2.5 - 5.5+ hrs/day) C (Constantly) Occupation requires this activity more than 66% of the time (5.5+ hrs/day) EOE Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4473758/Benedictine-College/Assistant-Director-of-Residence-Life-for-Student-Conduct": {
      "title": "Benedictine College - Assistant Director of Residence Life for Student Conduct",
      "description": "Benedictine College - Assistant Director of Residence Life for Student Conduct In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Assistant Director of Residence Life for Student Conduct Benedictine College Apply Assistant Director of Residence Life for Student Conduct Atchison, KS Apply Description Department: Student Life Job Status: Full-time; 12-month position FLSA Status: E xempt Reports To: Director of Residence Life Grade/Level: Amount of Travel Required: Minimal travel required Work Schedule: 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM; some night and weekend work Positions Supervised: Residence Hall Directors (Student Conduct situations) POSITION SUMMARY The Assistant Director of Residence Life assists the Director of Residence Life in providing leadership of the residence life program for over 2,200 resident students and non-resident students in a manner that complements the mission of Benedictine College and as a team member of the Student Life Office. Assists the Director in the formation of students and helps set the tone for much of the student experience outside the classroom. This position is the primary administrator of student conduct at the college and independently evaluates student conduct cases, determines appropriate sanctions, investigates or oversees investigations, resolves student conduct matters, and enforces sanctions in a manner consistent with College policies. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Lead the administration of all student conduct cases to ensure the effective application of student handbook policies and fundamental fairness to students engaged in the student conduct process. Serve as a primary adjudicator for documented incidents of policy violations and referrals to the office of student conduct, independently evaluate all evidence in cases and make the appropriate disciplinary decisions and enforce sanctions, including the sanctions of suspension or dismissal. Manage the student conduct database (Maxient), from report through resolution, including intake, documentation, communication, case management, user administration, and record maintenance. Provide oversight of student conduct cases including case management support and training for Residence Life staff. Establish, implement, and oversee a student conduct board, including recruitment, training, supervision, and ongoing development of board members. Support the administration of the Title IX policy, including collecting and referring reports and serving in the roles of Title IX investigator and advisor. Collaborates with the Vice Provost of Student Affairs, Director of Residence Life and the Director of security to ensure compliance with Clery, Title IX, and VAWA requirements. Facilitate the ongoing review, revision, and implementation of the Student Code of Conduct. Assist the Director of Residence Life with leadership, vision, administration for Student Housing and residential life programs, staff and facilities, in collaboration with other campus offices and departments. Assist in ensuring that safety and security procedures are established and maintained. Assist the Director of Residence Life in setting the tone for the implementation of a residential environment that reflects our Catholic beliefs and culture, is positive and engaging, and challenges students’ growth as young adults. Assist with the hiring, training, and supervising residential life staff and operations. Lead the summer housing programming, including housing assignment management, and the hiring, training, and supervision of the Resident Director and Resident Assistants. Assist in developing and providing programs and services which address emerging student concerns and needs. Provide on-call consultation and/or response for emergency situations. Assist in responding to questions, concerns, requests and complaints from residents, parents, and the college community. This is not an inclusive list of duties and responsibilities, and the individual will be assigned other essential duties as the need occurs. Requirements POSITION QUALIFICATIONS Competency Statement(s) Understanding and acceptance of Catholic and Benedictine values Demonstrated experience in developing and implementing programs Thorough knowledge of higher education student development, formation, risk management, and legal issues Ability to relate effectively with students, parents, faculty and staff Excellent oral, written and interpersonal skills as well as proven administrative and organizational skills Computer skills including word processing, e-mail and database software Education Strong understanding of and ability to weave a formational approach into various types of initiatives and an ability to foster a balanced Catholic culture. Master’s degree preferred in relevant field Experience Two to three years related experience working in a related area on a college campus. Residence Life and/or Student Life experience preferred Demonstrated experience in formation and the ability to foster a balanced Catholic culture. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Physical Abilities Stand F Walk F Sit F Handling / Fingering F Reach Outward F Reach Above Shoulder O Climb O Crawl N Squat or Kneel O Bend F Push / Pull 12 lbs or less O 13-25 lbs O 26-40 lbs O 41-100 lbs N Lift /Carry 10 lbs or less C 11-20 lbs O 21-50 lbs O 51-100 lbs N Over 100 lbs N N (Not Applicable) Activity is not applicable to this occupation. O (Occasionally) Occupation requires this activity up to 33% of the time (0 - 2.5+ hrs/day) F (Frequently) Occupation requires this activity from 33% - 66% of the time (2.5 - 5.5+ hrs/day) C (Constantly) Occupation requires this activity more than 66% of the time (5.5+ hrs/day) EOE Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
