    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4316304/Benedictine-College/Senior-Accountant": {
      "title": "In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript.",
      "description": "Benedictine College - Senior Accountant In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Senior Accountant Benedictine College Apply Senior Accountant Atchison, KS Apply Description Department: Business Office Job Status: Full-time FLSA Status : Exempt Reports To: Controller Amount of Travel Required: Typically none; occasional travel may be required. Work Schedule: M-F 8:00am – 5:00pm CST Positions Supervised: May supervise student workers or accounting assistants as assigned Position Summary: The Business Office of Benedictine College seeks a detail-oriented and highly skilled Senior Accountant to support the financial operations of the College. This role is responsible for maintaining accurate financial records, supporting budgeting and forecasting activities, ensuring compliance with institutional policies and applicable regulations, and assisting with audit preparation and reporting requirements. The Senior Accountant will play a key role in establishing financial processes and internal controls for Benedictine College, ensuring fiscal integrity and operational efficiency in a growing academic environment. The ideal candidate has strong accounting experience, excellent analytical & communication skills, and the ability to work independently in a fast-paced and developing organizational structure. Requirements Essential Functions: Participate in the day-to-day accounting operations for Benedictine College, including journal entries, reconciliations, and month-end & year-end close processes. Assist in the development, monitoring, and analysis of the College’s operating and restricted budgets. Prepare financial reports, forecasts, and variance analyses for leadership review and decision-making. Ensure compliance with institutional policies, GAAP standards, and applicable federal, state, and accreditation-related financial requirements. Support audit preparation, and coordinate with external auditors as needed throughout the entire audit process. Maintain accurate general ledger accounts and ensure proper classification of revenues and expenditures. Assist in the development and implementation of financial procedures, internal controls, and best practices for Benedictine College. Process and review financial transactions for grants, including reimbursements, procurement activity, and expense reporting for both accuracy and compliance. Collaborate with institutional finance and accounting offices to ensure alignment with college-wide financial systems and reporting standards. Provide financial guidance and support to department leadership, faculty administrators, and staff. Assist in the preparation of the annual form 990. Also, provide support for federal & state tax returns, which includes serving as a liaison with external tax accountants. Serve as insurance liaison for the College to assist with filing claims, policy & pricing updates, address campus-wide insurance inquiries, and assist departments to ensure risk exposure is appropriately mitigated. Also manages the Workers Compensation audit function related to vendors providing proof of insurance to the College. Interface with bond legal counsel to ensure full compliance with all bond covenants. Coordinate with other Business Office employees who support this particular endeavor indirectly through their work. Responsibilities include calculating & analyzing ratios, while monitoring UBI compliance due to bond covenants. Calculate ratio forecasting and analysis for external reporting and Finance Committee presentations, including drafting variance explanations related to such ratios and analysis. General ledger maintenance. This includes creating and managing general ledger accounts, including closing the ledger annually. Monitor grant and restricted fund activity, ensuring proper documentation and compliance with funding requirements, including reporting to appropriate external agencies as well as for the annual audit.  Liaison with various departments that are beneficiaries of grant monies, to collaborate on requirements from application through final reporting. Supervise student workers or entry-level accounting support staff, as assigned. Provide informal feedback and coaching when needed. Perform other duties, as assigned, in support of the financial integrity and mission of Benedictine College. This may include special projects or dedicated research to draw conclusions or analysis for management. Position Qualifications: Experience: Minimum of 5 years of progressive accounting or finance experience required. Experience in higher education, healthcare, or nonprofit accounting strongly preferred. Experience with budgeting, audits, and fund accounting highly desirable. Prior experience supporting a new program or organizational startup is a plus. Skills & Abilities: Strong knowledge of accounting principles and financial reporting standards (GAAP). Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a complex environment. Strong attention to detail and accuracy in financial data. Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and financial systems (Ellucian Colleague & Paylocity) Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and exercise sound judgment. Writing Skills: Ability to prepare clear and professional financial reports and summaries. May be required to complete a technical accounting exercise for finalists. Education: Required: Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field. Preferred: Master’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or Business Administration. Preferred: CPA designation or progress toward CPA certification. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Physical Abilities Stand O Walk O Sit C Handling / Fingering O Reach Outward O Reach Above Shoulder O Climb N Crawl N Squat or Kneel O Bend O Push / Pull 12 lbs or less O 13-25 lbs O 26-40 lbs N 41-100 lbs N Lift /Carry 10 lbs or less O 11-20 lbs O 21-50 lbs N 51-100 lbs N Over 100 lbs N N (Not Applicable) Activity is not applicable to this occupation. O (Occasionally) Occupation requires this activity up to 33% of the time (0 - 2.5+ hrs/day) F (Frequently) Occupation requires this activity from 33% - 66% of the time (2.5 - 5.5+ hrs/day) C (Constantly) Occupation requires this activity more than 66% of the time (5.5+ hrs/day) EOE Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4336034/Benedictine-College/Grounds-Lawncare-Technician": {
      "title": "Benedictine College - Grounds & Lawncare Technician",
      "description": "Benedictine College - Grounds & Lawncare Technician In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Grounds & Lawncare Technician Benedictine College Apply Grounds & Lawncare Technician Atchison, KS Apply Description Department: Operations Job Status: Full-time FLSA Status: Non-exempt Reports To: Grounds Supervisor Work Schedule: Daytime; evenings and weekends as needed Amount of Travel Required: Minimal Positions Supervised: None The Grounds Team maintains the campus lawns, landscapes, sports fields, concrete, water features, etc. in a manner that reflects the highest levels of professionalism. This includes mowing, trimming, trash removal, trimming trees and shrubs, planting flowers, fertilizing, and general landscape maintenance. Must be very experienced in lawn care and landscape maintenance. We offer: Paid vacation Paid holidays Sick time off Healthcare Insurance Dental Insurance Vision Insurance 401k with 5% match after one year of employment Full time hours (7am - 330pm or 6am – 230pm) Biweekly pay starting at $20 per hour Requirements ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Valid driver’s license Drug-Free Educational background in Horticulture, Turf science, Irrigation Repair or Landscape Maintenance . Perform lawn care services, including fertilization, weed control, aeration, seeding, etc. The ability to work independently and/or part of a team Provide a professional and creative service to improve the appearance of our campus Professional appearance Excellent oral communication skills Problem Solving Ability to lift or carry up to 50 pounds (8-10) hours per day Able and willing to work in various weather conditions (8-10) hours per day Snow removal in the Winter Landscape bed maintenance, shrub trimming and tree trimming. Mowing 1 to 2 days per week with a zero-turn mower is possible. Willing to learn and be certified on a Bobcat skid steer. Ability to work well with others, take direction & be self-motivated. Positive attitude with good people skills Have pride in your workmanship, detail oriented Additional duties to be assigned by the Grounds Supervisor, Landscape Coordinator, or Director of Operations. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS Competency Statements Accountability - Accountability looks at the extent to which an individual is willing to accept responsibility. Customer Oriented - Customer orientation implies a desire to serve both external and internal clients by focusing effort on meeting the client’s needs, understanding their concerns, and seeking to build trust. Detail Oriented - Detail orientation looks at the ability of the individual to pay meticulous attention to all aspects of a situation or task, no matter how small or seemingly unimportant. This competency asks the question “How well do you?” Time Management - Time management skills looks at the ability of the individual to effectively utilize available time for the completion of necessary job tasks. Working Under Pressure - Working under pressure looks at the ability of the individual to maintain composure when exposed to stress. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Physical Abilities Stand C Walk C Sit O Handling / Fingering C Reach Outward C Reach Above Shoulder F Climb F Crawl F Squat or Kneel F Bend C Push / Pull 12 lbs or less C 13-25 lbs F 26-40 lbs F 41-100 lbs O Lift /Carry 10 lbs or less C 11-20 lbs C 21-50 lbs F 51-100 lbs F Over 100 lbs O N (Not Applicable) Activity is not applicable to this occupation. O (Occasionally) Occupation requires this activity up to 33% of the time (0 - 2.5+ hrs/day) F (Frequently) Occupation requires this activity from 33% - 66% of the time (2.5 - 5.5+ hrs/day) C (Constantly) Occupation requires this activity more than 66% of the time (5.5+ hrs/day) EOE Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
